From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 07:51:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: mt6797: do not write through empty codec arrays

The front-end links use COMP_DUMMY(), which leaves the codec array empty
until the core fills in the dummy. The probe still writes the codec node
through dai_link->codecs on those links, into whatever follows the
zero-length array. In the built module that is the platform entry of
another link: playback_2_codecs and playback_1_platforms share an address.

Playback_1 therefore binds the MT6351 as its platform instead of the AFE,
snd_soc_rtdcom_lookup() finds no "mtk-afe-pcm" component, and hw_params
dereferences NULL in mtk_memif_set_rate_substream().

Skip links that have no codec entries.
---
 sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-mt6351.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-mt6351.c b/sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-mt6351.c
index a904398..fbb7e70 100644
--- a/sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-mt6351.c
+++ b/sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-mt6351.c
@@ -231,7 +231,11 @@ static int mt6797_mt6351_dev_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		goto put_platform_node;
 	}
 	for_each_card_prelinks(card, i, dai_link) {
-		if (dai_link->codecs->name)
+		/*
+		 * A COMP_DUMMY() codec array has no entries, so its address
+		 * belongs to whatever object the linker placed next.
+		 */
+		if (!dai_link->num_codecs || dai_link->codecs->name)
 			continue;
 		dai_link->codecs->of_node = codec_node;
 	}
